Sticky Widget was created by John K J Francis <johnkjfrancis@gmail.com>.

His is the idea, the product design, the interaction and visual design, and
the architecture the code follows. The design documents in this repository —
SPEC.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, and the decisions recorded in docs/ — describe his
choices, including several of the harder ones:

  - dragging a task from one note window into another, across two separate
    webviews, using native hit-testing rather than a web drag API that cannot
    leave its own window;
  - keeping one SQLite cache and one sync manager in the Rust core, with every
    note window as a view of it, rather than a copy of the state per window;
  - formatting descriptions as the plain text Google actually stores, so the
    phone and the web app never see something the widget invented;
  - naming what the Google Tasks API does not offer instead of hiding it.

The code was written by Claude (Anthropic) under his direction, to his review,
and through his repeated refinement.

